<!-- What Is Acoustic Drylining -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">What Is Acoustic Drylining?</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Acoustic drylining is a specialist construction system designed to significantly reduce sound transmission between rooms and spaces. Unlike standard drylining, which focuses on speed and cost-effectiveness, acoustic drylining prioritises sound insulation using a combination of dense plasterboard, sound-absorbing insulation, and carefully designed construction details.</p>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A well-designed acoustic drylining system can reduce sound transmission by 45 to 52 dB, transforming a noisy, distracting space into one that is calm, quiet, and private. At <strong>Drylining Edinburgh</strong>, we use proven construction methods and certified acoustic products to deliver consistent, measurable sound reduction for every project across Edinburgh, Leith, and the wider Lothians.</p>

<!-- What We Offer -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Our Acoustic Drylining Services</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Acoustic wall drylining with Gyproc Soundbloc and mineral wool</li>
  <li>Double-layer acoustic board systems for maximum performance</li>
  <li>Resilient channel and decoupling systems for superior sound isolation</li>
  <li>Acoustic ceiling drylining to reduce impact and airborne noise</li>
  <li>Soundproof partition walls for offices, meeting rooms, and home offices</li>
  <li>Joint sealing and acoustic sealant application to prevent sound leaks</li>
  <li>Upgrading existing walls to acoustic specifications</li>
  <li>Acoustic door and service penetration sealing</li>
</ul>

<!-- Why Acoustic Drylining -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Why Choose Acoustic Drylining?</h2>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li><strong>Significantly quieter rooms:</strong> Acoustic drylining reduces noise transmission by 45-52 dB, making rooms noticeably quieter and more private.</li>
  <li><strong>Scottish Building Standards compliant:</strong> All our acoustic installations meet Scottish Building Standards Section 4 (Sound) requirements for residential, commercial, and student accommodation.</li>
  <li><strong>Perfect for Edinburgh tenements:</strong> Edinburgh's New Town and Old Town tenements can be particularly noisy between flats. Acoustic drylining solves shared-wall sound transfer effectively.</li>
  <li><strong>Minimal space loss:</strong> Modern acoustic drylining systems deliver excellent sound reduction with only 50-100 mm of added wall thickness.</li>
  <li><strong>Smooth finish:</strong> The finished surface is smooth and ready for decoration, indistinguishable from standard drylining.</li>
  <li><strong>Suitable for all property types:</strong> Whether you have a Victorian tenement flat, a modern new build, or a commercial office, we can design an acoustic drylining system that delivers the performance you need.</li>
</ul>

<!-- Materials & Specifications -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Materials &amp; Specifications</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">We use premium acoustic materials from trusted manufacturers to ensure your drylining delivers the sound performance and durability you need.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Gyproc Soundbloc acoustic plasterboard</li>
  <li>Acoustic mineral wool insulation (Rockwool, Isover)</li>
  <li>Resilient channels and decoupling frames</li>
  <li>Acoustic sealants and acoustic gaskets</li>
  <li>Double-layer board systems for maximum performance</li>
  <li>Standard and moisture-resistant plasterboard where required</li>
</ul>

<!-- Applications & Use Cases -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">Applications &amp; Use Cases</h2>
<p style="font-size:1.0625rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Our acoustic drylining services are suitable for a wide range of building types and project sizes across Edinburgh.</p>
<ul style="list-style:disc;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
  <li>Victorian and Georgian tenement flat soundproofing (New Town, Old Town)</li>
  <li>Home office noise reduction in residential properties</li>
  <li>Music studio and recording room acoustics</li>
  <li>Meeting room and boardroom soundproofing in commercial offices</li>
  <li>Student accommodation acoustic walls</li>
  <li>Hotel room soundproofing</li>
  <li>Flats sharing party walls (Morningside, Bruntsfield, Stockbridge)</li>
  <li>School and education building acoustic treatment</li>
</ul>

<!-- How It Works -->
<h2 style="font-size:1.75rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--secondary);margin:2.5rem 0 1rem;">How It Works</h2>
<ol style="list-style:decimal;padding-left:1.5rem;color:var(--text);line-height:1.8;font-size:1.0625rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem;">
